    dt-bindings: power: supply: qcom,smbb: describe gadget-managed input
    
    Describe the explicit PM8226 opt-in for gadget-managed USB input limits.
    Initialize its input at the conservative budget and expose programmed
    and effective limits as read-only userspace attributes. Reject a
    conflicting manual USB limit and opt-in on unsupported charger variants.
    
    Carry the power-supply portion of Timothy Schmidt's d10a194d04f0 with
    Codex:GPT-6 assistance. The controller reference and consumer are a
    separate USB subsystem change.

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/supply/qcom,pm8941-charger.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/supply/qcom,pm8941-charger.yaml
index 6db552f16387..4b4044bb61f7 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/supply/qcom,pm8941-charger.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/supply/qcom,pm8941-charger.yaml
@@ -11,6 +11,14 @@ maintainers:
 
 allOf:
   - $ref: power-supply.yaml#
+  - if:
+      required:
+        - qcom,usb-gadget-current-limit
+    then:
+      properties:
+        compatible:
+          const: qcom,pm8226-charger
+        usb-charge-current-limit: false
 
 properties:
   qcom,software-charge-control:
@@ -20,6 +28,13 @@ properties:
       already be inhibited before native dependencies can defer probe. The
       parent keeps charging off until its policy child validates fresh inputs.
 
+  qcom,usb-gadget-current-limit:
+    type: boolean
+    description: |
+      Let the USB gadget controller manage the PM8226 USB input limit.
+      Initialize the limit to 100000 uA and expose the effective and
